A||||20||Krashdavus||Carpet Replacement??||||5||
Z||000000||Krashdavus||11-22-2001||02:26 PM||||I'm considering replacing the floor carpets in my '88 GT, partially due to leakage from the Clutch master cylinder.  I have the salt and pepper carpet, grey.  Doesn't seem to be made anymore.  I many have to buy a solid tone and redo the door trim.  I know they come in two bucket arrangments, anyone ever done this and how difficult is it.  I've done a carpet in Mustang recently and that was pudd, but this swap concerns me.  Any recomended sources??||||reg||5
Z||000001||Daleford||11-22-2001||02:48 PM||||Hey Krash, fellow Canadian here.   I am building a kitcar and have some left over parts from an 86. I believe I have an original salt and pepper carpet in great shape [no holes, rips, tears, etc] $50 plus shipping. Should be the same.<BR>By the way, what is pudd?<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||Phil||11-22-2001||03:06 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.accmats.com" TARGET=_blank>www.accmats.com</A>  sell the salt and pepper replacement carpets BUT <A HREF="http://www.1aautomotive.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.1aautomotive.com/</A>  sells the ACC stuff cheaper than ACC||||reg||1
Z||000003||Krashdavus||11-22-2001||03:29 PM||||Daleford: Pudd goes back to my college days at GMI, in a word - EASY.<P>I'm in Whitby, Ontario, you nearby?  E-mail me at hemicuda@sprint.ca<P>Phil, thanks for the reply.  I tried ACC and they cant' get it, I'll try the other place.<BR>However, our dollar here in Canada is drowning, a $150 Carpet is gonna cost me big bucks, not to mention bringing it x-border.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Spiff||11-22-2001||04:38 PM||||Krashdavus<P>You can get the A1Auto carpets on E-Bay for $109. That's what I paid and they have a set on there now for $115 U.S. They go on very easy and fit very well and look great. Hope this helps.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_4.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Spiff (edited 11-25-2001).]||||reg||1
