Z||000006||Krashdavus||11-23-2001||12:38 PM||||Class of '87 Nashco.  Mech. Eng. with a minor in Facilites Engineering.  GDI, fratboys were d*cks!.||||reg||6
Z||000007||Last Dodo||11-25-2001||10:00 PM||||I got my carpet from the Fierostore, and other than a little cutting it went in really easy.  I had to replace it after my wife left the windows partially opened on the freeway when we had to evac for a hurricane (really long story).  I would recommend buying a carpet knife at a local hardware store to simplify the job, unless you are going to get the carpet from Daleford.  Also check your padding while you are at it otherwise the job could take a lot longer than you may want (I drove for a week with no carpet while I waited for time to install the new padding and carpet).  Good luck!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Last Dodo (edited 11-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Nashco||11-25-2001||11:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Krashdavus:<BR><B>Class of '87 Nashco.  Mech. Eng. with a minor in Facilites Engineering.  GDI, fratboys were d*cks!.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ha, crazy!  I've met two alumni in the past week on the forum...lol.  I'm a soph II, ME Auto-Powertrain.  GDI as well...fratguys do suck..lol.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||rogergarrison||11-26-2001||02:51 AM||||Mostly the job is just taking out the seats,belts, and the strip of trim along the bottom of door. It just lays in there, no gluing. May need some minor trimming. FieroLisa did both sides of hers by herself in an hour.||||reg||1
Z||000010||CJ||11-26-2001||01:02 PM||||Haven't heard "pudd" since my college days at GMI (Class of 1975).  Also own an 88 GT that needs carpeting, thanks for the lead.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Neal||11-26-2001||07:49 PM||||Where should i look for black carpet?  Anywhere cheaper than the fierostore?||||reg||1
Z||000012||Spiff||11-26-2001||10:05 PM||||Go to E-Bay and buy it from A1 Auto. They sell it for $109. Alot cheaper than their web site. You can get any color you want. That's where I got my carpet and it looks very good. Installs in about an hour. Most of the time is spent taking the trim off and then putting it back on.<P><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_5.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||72vinman||11-26-2001||11:20 PM||||Hey Spiff, what model carpet did you order from A1. They have 4 kinds.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin2_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Spiff||11-26-2001||11:48 PM||||72vinman:<P>I used the custom comfort. They don't have cut pile anymore. It looks very good and install very easy. You can get any color you want. Hope this helps.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/spiffsig2_6.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Spiff (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
